(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #103: a thing holding text is still a value. A text
 is never changed in place; every sentence that changes one points its
 slot at another text. So after a copy, each way of writing a text
 field, on either side of the copy, is seen only by the side written:
 Set to a literal, Set to a format string, Set to a text variable, a
 bare `is`, and a whole-thing assignment back over the original.)

A thing called letter has
  a text called greeting is "dear friend",
  a text called signature.

a letter called original.
Set original's signature to "Ada".
a letter called reply is original.
Set original's signature to "Ada Lovelace".
Print original's signature.
Print reply's signature.

Set reply's greeting to "{reply's greeting}, again".
Print original's greeting.
Print reply's greeting.

a text called borrowed is "Grace".
Set reply's signature to borrowed.
Set borrowed to "{borrowed} Hopper".
Print original's signature.
Print reply's signature.
Print borrowed.

original's greeting is "to whom it may concern".
Print original.
Print reply.

Set original to reply.
Set reply's signature to "changed after the copy back".
Print original.
Print reply.
